      "message": "The PS3 test failures were from 2 issues that are now fixed;\n- $apply_ootf had been skipping work when w \u003e 0, but the original code (and what needs to happen) is to only skip work when w \u003d 0. Negative w\u0027s are perfectly valid. This was breaking certain HLG conversions because we stopped applying the ootf step when we should have bene.\n- Asserts firing when compiling RTE that used the to/fromLinearSRGB functions: I had said in the commit message and assumed in the assert that we were always specializing these, but RuntimeEffectBlock::HandleIntrinsics needed to be updated to do so so the nodes were containing the unexpected PreAlpha/PostAlpha blocks that are always no-ops for these functions.\n\nAlso addressed all of Rob\u0027s feedback, barring resolving the question about versioning the serialized keys.",
